Copyright 2004-2021 The Apache Software Foundation.

These messages are used in mime/tests/test_rfc_conformance_mime4j.cpp,
which asserts libglot's own verified parsing behavior for each fixture
(not a byte-for-byte reproduction of mime4j's own expected-output XML,
since mime4j's internal tree model and leniency choices sometimes differ
from libglot's by design -- see that file's comments for specifics).
